# STB Security — Architecture Documentation

## 1. Project Overview

**STB Security** is a web-based security agent management system built for **Société Tunisienne de Banque (STB)**. It manages security agents, their site assignments, daily attendance tracking, reports, and leave/ticket requests across three role levels: Admin, Team Leader (Chef d'Équipe), and Agent.

---

## 2. Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|-----------|
| Frontend | Angular 19 (TypeScript, standalone components) |
| Backend | Node.js + Express.js (REST API) |
| Database | PostgreSQL (via `pg` library) |
| Authentication | JWT (JSON Web Tokens, 24h expiry) + bcrypt password hashing |
| Map | Leaflet (OpenStreetMap tiles) |
| HTTP Client | Angular HttpClient with functional interceptor |

---

## 3. Roles & Permissions

### Role Levels

| Role | Level | Description |
|------|-------|-------------|
| `agent` | 1 | Security guard — view own profile, assignments, attendance, submit tickets |
| `chef_equipe` | 2 | Team leader — manage agents, attendance, reports, approve tickets |
| `admin` | 3 | Full system administrator — manage sites, users, agents, everything |

Permission hierarchy: `admin` (3) ≥ `chef_equipe` (2) ≥ `agent` (1). Higher level inherits lower level access.

