## 8. Authentication Flow

```
┌─────────┐     POST /api/auth/login      ┌──────────┐    SELECT * FROM users    ┌──────────┐
│  Login   │ ──── { email, password } ────→│  Express  │ ──────────────────────→│ Postgres │
│  Page    │                                │  Backend  │ ←── { user } ──────────│          │
└─────────┘                                └──────────┘                        └──────────┘
     │                                            │
     │     ←── { token, user } ──                 │
     │                                            │
     ▼                                            │
┌──────────────────┐                              │
│  localStorage    │                              │
│  setItem(token)  │                              │
│  currentUser$    │                              │
│  .next(user)     │                              │
└──────────────────┘                              │
     │                                            │
     ▼                                            │
┌──────────────────┐     Each HTTP request        │
│  AuthInterceptor │ ──── Authorization: Bearer   │
│  (HttpInterceptorFn)     <token> ──────────────→│
└──────────────────┘                              │
     │                                            │
     ▼                                            │
┌──────────────────┐     jwt.verify(token)        │
│  auth.js         │ ←────────────────────────────│
│  (middleware)    │     req.user = decoded        │
└──────────────────┘                              │
     │                                            │
     ▼                                            │
┌──────────────────┐  roles.js: compares level    │
│  roles.js        │  userLevel >= requiredLevel  │
│  (middleware)    │                              │
└──────────────────┘                              │
     │                                            │
     ▼                                            │
┌──────────────────┐                              │
│  Route Handler   │ ──── SQL query ─────────────→│
└──────────────────┘                              │
```

### JWT Payload Structure

```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "email": "agent@stb.tn",
  "role": "agent",
  "iat": 1700000000,
  "exp": 1700086400
}
```

### Flow Steps

1. User submits credentials on login page
2. Backend verifies email/password against `users` table (bcrypt compare)
3. Backend signs JWT with `JWT_SECRET` (24h expiry)
4. Frontend stores token in `localStorage('token')`
5. `AuthService.currentUser$` BehaviorSubject emits decoded user
6. `AuthInterceptorFn` clones every `HttpRequest` with `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
7. `AuthGuard` checks token existence before allowing route navigation
8. On page refresh: `AuthService` constructor decodes JWT locally (immediate role for navbar), then calls `GET /api/auth/me` for full user data (including `agent_id`)
9. `roles.js` middleware uses hierarchical level comparison — admin (3) can access chef (2) and agent (1) routes

